{
  "opening": "This release introduces significant enhancements to the glom library, focusing on new specification types, improved CLI capabilities, and better introspection. The public API now exposes several new spec classes and functions that allow for more flexible data transformation and error handling.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m15",
      "text": "The `glom_cli` command-line interface must accept Python full specifications rather than just AST literals, allowing complex expressions in specs. When a target is provided as an AST literal via the CLI, it must be correctly parsed and processed by `mw_handle_target`."
    },
    {
      "id": "m29",
      "text": "The release must expose the `Auto`, `Fill`, `Iter`, and `Let` spec classes, along with the `ROOT` constant, as part of the public API. These names must be accessible directly from the main module namespace alongside existing exports like `Spec` and `TType`."
    },
    {
      "id": "m34",
      "text": "The `Invoke` class must remain publicly available under the name `Invoke`. The module-level constants previously known as `consts` are now exclusively exposed as `constants`, ensuring backward compatibility if `consts` is removed or deprecated."
    },
    {
      "id": "m44",
      "text": "The `Fill` spec class must provide a meaningful string representation when its `__repr__` method is called, returning a string that clearly identifies it as a Fill instance."
    },
    {
      "id": "m45",
      "text": "The `Assign` spec class and the `assign` function must both have implemented `__repr__` methods that return descriptive strings identifying their respective types."
    },
    {
      "id": "m46",
      "text": "The `Coalesce` spec class and the `Inspect` spec class must implement `__repr__` methods that return clear, identifiable string representations of these objects."
    },
    {
      "id": "m47",
      "text": "All public spec types, including `Auto` and `Check`, must have functional `__repr__` methods that return strings uniquely identifying each spec type for debugging purposes."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure all new public names are properly exported and documented. Verify that the CLI changes do not break existing workflows using AST literal targets."
}
